  "card": "This PR simplifies AddrMan timestamp updates and fixes a multiplicity calculation flaw for gossip announcements. It removes the legacy 1-hour/24-hour update throttling rule, updating address timestamps whenever newer information arrives since AddrMan operations now occur in memory. It also subtracts the gossip time penalty when comparing an incoming announcement against an existing entry, preventing identical announcements relayed across multiple peers from appearing newer than the stored penalized record. The author notes this fixes an unintended multiplicity increase in benign multi-hop gossip relay rather than serving as an adversarial defense.",
